  "from": "2026-04",
  "description": "Fuselage: Navy blue crown and upper fuselage with scattered white stars (13 stars); a broad red band sweeps along the lower fuselage from the nose to the tail; cream/off-white belly; huge white quill-script '1776' over the forward fuselage; script 'life, liberty and the pursuit of Happiness' in white on the aft fuselage. Cheatlines: Red sweep with thin cream edge. Tail: NOT the Heart tail: white fin with a red band along the leading edge/top and navy blue lower fin carrying white 'Southwest'. Engines: Navy with a circle of white stars (Betsy Ross flag) on each cowling. Winglets: Navy with America250 decal. Titles: White 'Southwest' on navy lower fin; 'America 250' logo on the nose; tail number 1776. Artwork: Declaration of Independence text; 13 stars. Colors hex: approximate.",
